  <data name="pmdorand/documentation:stat/mode=r">
    <value>
      The randomized value must be within an exact distance from the original value.
      For example, if the original value is 50 and the Range Value is 25, the randomized value is limited to between 25 and 75.
    </value>
  </data>

  <data name="pmdorand/documentation:stat/mode=e">
    <value>
      The randomized value must be within a percentage-based distance from the original value.
      For example, if the original value is 50 and the Range Value is 100, the randomized value is limited to between 0 and 100.
    </value>
  </data>

  <data name="pmdorand/documentation:stat/mode=a">
    <value>
      The randomized value can be anything between the minimum and maximum limits, but the original value is replaced by the range.
      For example, if the Range Value is set to 25, and the range is [0, 255], the randomized value can be anything between 0 and 255, but pulled towards/away from 25.
    </value>
  </data>



